> Another question is that why isn't Patchhack bones recognised by Hearse?

None of the individual patches mentioned on the patchhack page should
break bones compatibility.. You mean the binary packet?
Maybe it has some compile-time option set different from the official
binaries, so that it affects bones compatibility. For example,
SCORE_ON_BOTL. (I have made a patch that makes the game hide it from bones
files and ignore it when checking compatibility:
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html#showscore )
Or maybe it was compiled with another compiler that aligns bytes
differently from the one used for the official binaries, and thus produces
different sizes for the critical structs.

